1 DIRECTORY
    The DIRECTORY command lists files on a mounted ODS-2 volume, laid out
    as VMS's DIRECTORY lays them out: a heading for each directory, the
    names four to a line (or one to a line, with the columns the
    qualifiers ask for), and "Total of n files." after each directory
    ("Grand total" after more than one).  A specification that finds no
    file is %DIRECT-W-NOFILES.

    Syntax:

        DIRECTORY [/FULL] [/FILE] [/SIZE[=option]] [/DATE] [/OWNER]
                  [/PROTECTION] [/VERSIONS=n] [/[NO]HEADING]
                  [/[NO]TRAILING] [/OUTPUT[=file]] [file-spec[,...]]

    Parameter:

        file-spec       The file specification to list, which may include
                        wildcards (e.g. DUA0:[MYDIR]*.TXT;*), or a list of
                        them, each listed in turn with one grand total
                        (e.g. [A...],[B...]).  Any part of
                        the specification left out is filled in from the
                        current default device/directory (see SET
                        DEFAULT), but a version left out is every
                        version.  If omitted entirely, lists "*.*;*" --
                        every file, every version, in the current default
                        directory.

    Qualifiers:

        /FULL           Shows everything the file's header says: its
                        file ID, used and allocated sizes, owner, dates,
                        organization, record format and attributes, and
                        protection.

        /FILE           Includes each file's file ID.

        /SIZE[=option]  Includes each file's size, in blocks: USED (the
                        default), ALLOCATION, or ALL (used/allocated).

        /DATE           Includes each file's creation date.

        /OWNER          Includes each file's owner, as [SYSTEM] or
                        [group,member].

        /PROTECTION     Includes each file's protection: the access
                        granted to system, owner, group, and world, in
                        that order, as in (RWED,RWED,RE,).

        /VERSIONS=n     Lists only the n most recent versions of each
                        file: /VERSIONS=1 shows just the newest.  The
                        value is required and must be at least 1.

        /NOHEADING      No "Directory" headings: each file is listed by
                        its full name, one to a line.

        /NOTRAILING     No totals.

        /OUTPUT[=file]  Writes the listing to a file in place of the
                        terminal: file (type LIS unless it gives one), or
                        DIRECTORY.LIS.  A specification that finds no file
                        still shows %DIRECT-W-NOFILES at the terminal.

    Examples:

        DIRECTORY

        DIRECTORY/VERSIONS=2 *.TXT;*

        DIRECTORY/SIZE *.TXT;*

        DIR DUA0:[MYDIR]

    See also the help for SET DEFAULT, SHOW DEFAULT, TYPE, and MOUNT.
